=============================================================================
# MM Dual-Antigen (BCMA/GPRC5D) escape analysis — Python rebuild
#
# Rule of thumb: commit source and small presentable outputs (tables, figures);
# never commit data or large regenerable binaries.
#
# NOTE ON DEPTH: patterns here are deliberately depth-independent (bare
# `*.h5ad`, not `results/*.h5ad`). A pattern like `results/*.rds` matches ONLY
# the top level, so `results/04_qc/foo.rds` would slip through — that exact gap
# previously let 638 MB of nested checkpoints stage in one commit. The pipeline
# writes into `results/NN_*/` subdirectories, so match by extension at any depth.
# =============================================================================




# --- Raw data (large, regenerable via scripts/01_download_data.sh) ------------
raw/*.tar
raw/unpacked/
raw/unpacked_bulk/
raw/samples/
raw/gtf/

# Keep the small manifest — it documents what was actually downloaded/found
!raw/sample_manifest.csv

# The GEO SOFT files are ~8 KB each and are the input to
# io.rebuild_sample_metadata_from_soft, so they are committed as provenance for
# resources/sample_metadata/. The XML and series-matrix encodings carry the same
# content in a bulkier form and are not.
!raw/*_family.soft.gz
raw/*_family.xml.tgz
raw/*_series_matrix.txt.gz

# --- Generated analysis outputs ----------------------------------------------
results/


# The paper's supplementary tables (Cancer Research CAN-22-1769), ~500 KB in total
# and committed for the same reason as the SOFT files: S1 is the input to
# io.rebuild_clinical_metadata_from_s1, and the others are the paper's own numbers
# that later stages are compared against. Which is which:
#   s1  Table S1  clinical characteristics + WashU-1 disease stage   PARSED, used
#   s2  Table S2  target novelty tiers / trial IDs for 37 antigens   stage 08/12 ref
#   s3  Table S3  38x38 target correlation + co-exp / mut-excl pairs stage 08 ref
#   s4  Table S4  NetMHC peptide-HLA binding                         not used here
#   s5  Table S6  recurrent mutations (different MMRF samples)       not used here
#   s6  Table S5  the paper's own bulk-vs-scRNA Pearson r per gene   stage 09 ref
# Note the last two files are numbered off-by-one against their in-file titles, and
# s5 is strict-OOXML so openpyxl reports zero sheets — it is not corrupt.
!raw/can-22-1769_table_s*.xlsx

# --- Large binary pipeline outputs, at any depth ------------------------------
# AnnData / HDF5 checkpoints, the bulk of what stages 04-12 produce
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.loom
*.zarr/
# Serialized intermediates
*.rds
*.RData
*.npy
*.npz
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib
*.feather
*.parquet
# Per-cell intermediate tables. These are one row per cell (172,940 of them), which
# is megabytes of CSV that is not a deliverable and is cheaply regenerable — the
# stage-05b labels take ~20 s from the committed model. Same call as stage 04, which
# deliberately writes no pooled obs table at all.
results/**/provisional_labels.csv

# Everything else under results/ (CSV, PNG, PDF, SVG, JSON, MD) is committed by
# default — those are the actual deliverables. No negation rules needed, since
# nothing above excludes a directory.

# --- Notebooks ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks are jupytext-paired (percent format). The paired `.py` is the
# committed, reviewable artifact; the `.ipynb` is a local build product with
# heavy embedded outputs. See CLAUDE.md's "Code structure" section.
#
# To commit notebooks instead, delete the line below and install nbstripout
# (`nbstripout --install`) so outputs are stripped on commit.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.jupyter/
.virtual_documents/

# --- Python artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Environments / package managers ------------------------------------------
.conda/
.mamba/
*.conda
.venv/
venv/
# conda envs created in-tree (`-p envs/<name>`); the envs/*.yml specs are source
envs/*/

# --- R artifacts (rpy2/scDblFinder bridge in env-qc still runs R) -------------
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
.Rprofile

# --- Scratch / local -----------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.log
# ...but a stage's run log is provenance — it records what actually executed,
# with which thresholds. The R build committed one and it earned its place.
!results/**/*.log
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Old/backup script versions ------------------------------------------------
scripts/__*.sh
scripts/__*.py

# --- OS / editor cruft ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- Session scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
# `claude --teleport <id>` handle, written per-session; not project source.
session_id.txt
